ually within 20 30 minutes  um the dilutions are performed on the  instrument so there's no waiting for the  three hour elisa to finish for the  dilution  um and the the the only sort of downfall  or maybe limitation is that it requires  the amino acid analyzer to perform that  assay for that specific vendor  and so those are just some things to  investigate if you're interested in  bringing fecal cal protectant in-house  and another thing that's important to  consider is the method of extraction so  extraction is the process of putting the  stool into some buffer and then  rigorously shaking it to extract the cow  protectant  from the stool  and so the gold standard is the manual  extraction process  and so what this  entails is that usually we do all of our  stool extractions within a hood  and so the technologist will stir the  stool because we like things well  homogenized and then we will mask out  usually about 100 migs of the stool  sample and then write down that specific  mass on that container and then dilute  it with an appropriate amount of buffer  and then that gets rigorously vortexed  and then it often has to undergo a  second dilution to be at the appropriate  concentration for the assay and it might  need a centrifugation  we're going to contrast that with the  device extraction  so the manufacturers have gotten very  creative and made many of these  extraction devices  and these are pre-filled tubes with  buffer and they have what we like to say  in my lab the magic wand  and the magic wand has these precision  grooves and these precision grooves  collects an accurate and precise amount  of stool and you can see i've i've just  shown some of the wands of different  extraction devices and just labeled how  much how many migs of stool they collect  and so it is much lower than the manual  weighing process  but the good thing about these devices  is that you know you poke it into a  homogenized dual sample stick it into  the device vortex it and then 